{
 "_doc": "Authored intent phrasings, merged into build/tools/aiconnect-capabilities.json by scripts/gen-capabilities.mjs. The AiConnect gateway folds these into its BM25 search haystack only - never into what the model is shown, and never into the embedding.",
 "_why": "Measured on the 122-task revit benchmark: +8.8 pt recall@1 and +10.0 pt weighted coverage for ~4.6 KB, with negative controls held at 6/8. For comparison the entire semantic/ONNX stack buys +4.4 pt recall@1 and +1.9 pt weighted for ~104 MB of vendored runtime plus a ~130 MB model download. Driver: aiconnector/scripts/bundle-benchmark/alias_ab.py",
 "_rule": "An alias must not introduce a word that is COMMON in ordinary English but RARE in the corpus. BM25 IDF treats such a word as maximally discriminating, so it becomes a magnet for queries the tool should refuse. Measured: the alias 'how much concrete is in the model' made 'Write me a haiku about concrete' match get_material_quantities at 3.05 and cost a negative control. Name the operation, not a material, a trade, or any everyday noun.",
